Test vectors for vlpds's Spaces primitives (src/space), from the reference
implementation:

  repo:    https://github.com/bluesky-social/atproto
  branch:  permissioned-data (the October 22 2026 alpha)
  commit:  ac0c9f15392f6f0298d71dc52aa88c05036150be
  release: 0.0.0-spaces-alpha-20261022141228 (@atproto/space, @atproto/crypto,
           @atproto/lex-data, @atproto/lex-cbor on npm, dist-tag alpha)

vectors.json was generated, not copied: the reference's own tests in
packages/space/tests use random keys and check round trips, and only
tests/lthash.test.ts pins vectors (the empty digest and add('one').add('two'),
both included in vectors.json and asserted on their own in src/space/lthash.rs).
gen-vectors.mjs produced it by running the published release (Node 24) with
fixed keys; see its header for how to re-run it. Each vector was verified by
the reference before it was written out: commits and their STAR metadata,
the KEM shared secret (decapsulate on both fixed keys), commit and record
MACs and both MAC headers, HTTP message signatures (createSpaceSigHeaders,
checked by verifyCredentialSig), tokens, and STAR archives (serializeRepo,
read back by verifyRepoStarFull). Only the token jtis are random, so a
re-run changes the `tokens` entries alone.

Syntax cases (src/lexicon.rs tests) are ported from
packages/syntax/tests/aturi-string.test.ts and
packages/lexicon/tests/general.test.ts; HTTP signature and token cases
(src/space/{httpsig,token}.rs tests) from packages/space/src/http-signature.test.ts
and packages/space/tests/credential.test.ts.

License: MIT (bluesky-social/atproto).

export.star and export.json (tests/all/spaces_side/import_repo.rs) are a space
repo as the reference PDS's com.atproto.space.getRepo serves it, generated by
gen-export.mjs with the same release: the reference's serializeRecord,
RepoCommit.toCommit and serializeRepo over five records (one naming a blob),
checked with verifyRepoStarFull before it was written. The output is
deterministic.
